<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">André Parrot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">André Parrot was a French archaeologist who directed the excavation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a> at Tell Hariri in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> from 1933 until 1974. His team uncovered the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimri-lim">Zimri-Lim</a>, temples, statues and some 20,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> tablets of the royal archives of Mari. He also excavated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girsu">Girsu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/larsa">Larsa</a> and was later director of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louvre">Louvre</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andre-parrot.jpg" alt="André Parrot" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harry Pot · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AndreParrot1961.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
